 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 521061,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b9b454662212da90.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Sarkar J, Potdar AA, Saidel GM/PLoS Computational Biology)\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>One process that is under the control of a negative feedback loop is red blood cell production. The hormone erythropoietin stimulates production of new blood cells. The graph shows erythropoietin levels after someone donates some blood.</p>\n<p>When is the red blood cell production at its maximum?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1018553,
     "content_html": "At day 0 mark."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018554,
     "content_html": "About 10 days after the blood donation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018555,
     "content_html": "About 20 days after the blood donation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1018556,
     "content_html": "After 40 days after the blood donation."
    }
   ],
